Z||000000||87GT||04-17-2000||02:56 PM||||When the Fiero was in production, I was only 6-10 years old and dont remember much about them.  I was watching a show today that showed a commercial from the past that featured a 78 Grand Prix and I got to thinking to myself, "What kind of Fiero commercials were there?  I dont remember any.  I dont think anybody here has mentioned anything about it.  Do you guys/gals remember em?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||04-17-2000||05:11 PM||||Bought my first Fiero new, in 85.<BR>But... I don't ever remember seeing any commercials. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||BN Boomer||04-17-2000||08:00 PM||||I just remember as a high school student in the mid 80s hearing that Fieros caught on fire all the time. ||||reg||10
Z||000003||Oreif||04-17-2000||08:51 PM||||The only one I remember seeing was the 1988 commercial that had a red GT driving thru a town at dusk. I think the song "Ride Pontiac Ride" played in the background and the "we build excitment" slogan was at the end.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierosound||04-17-2000||10:42 PM||||The only Fiero commercial I ever remember seeing was for the GT (86-88 style) when it came out...<P>A "Bond" type guy in a tuxedo, comes out of what appears to be a Monte Carlo Casino.  The doorman (an older gent) signals for his car.  A valet pulls up in a Red/Grey GT with aero nose and wing, gets out and hands him his keys.<BR> <BR>The doorman, admiring the car, asks "Is it Italian?"<P>Bond guy: "No"<P>Doorman: "German?" <P>Bong guy: "No"<P>Doorman "Japanese?"<P>Bond guy: "No, (pause), It's a Pontiac".<P>The Bond guy then hops in the car, fires it up, and roars off.  The camera zooms in and catches the lit-up PONTIAC in the rear tail lights as it roars by.<P>END<P><BR>The commercial was impressive and well shot.  The GT looked and sounded great.  Wish I had it on video... <BR>  <p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 04-17-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000005||Cooter||04-17-2000||10:47 PM||||I have some old Sledgehammer and Max-Headroom shows on tape around here somewhere. I will check them out and see if there are any Fiero adds in there.||||reg||1
